------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS BUILT
------------------------------------------------------------
A production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic parity of the web VIN-decoder devtool, decomposed
one-responsibility-per-file (mirrors the TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets convention):

  VinDecoder.Adapter.swift   pure Foundation decode core (VinField, VinBreakdown, VinDecoderAdapter
                             + the five VIN_* lookup tables). Shared-free and SwiftUI-free → host-
                             compiles + unit-tests in isolation. Parity with the web `useMemo`.
  VinDecoder.Model.swift     P1/S11 telemetry seam (VinDecoderTelemetry + OSLogVinDecoderTelemetry
                             emitting `view.opened surface=VinDecoder`), @Observable VinDecoderModel
                             (holds `vin`, derives `phase`), P1/S10 i18n facade (VinDecoderStrings,
                             table "VinDecoder"), testable VinDecoderAccessibility summary.
  VinDecoder.swift           VinDecoderView surface — ToolCard chrome (car icon + title + desc),
                             input, content switch, lifecycle (onAppear→start / onDisappear→stop),
                             surfaceSlug = "VinDecoder".
  VinDecoder.Content.swift   VinInputField (@Bindable), VinDecodedGrid (responsive 2-col), VinFieldCell,
                             VinEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView).
  VinDecoder.Previews.swift  #Preview empty / decoded / decoded-with-unknown-segments (DEBUG).
  VinDecoder.Tests.swift     XCTest: adapter + model + telemetry + i18n facade + accessibility.
  VinDecoder.strings         P1/S10 catalog (15 keys): the exact web keys ("Vin Decoder",
                             "Vin Decoder Desc", "Vin", "Unknown", devtools.utils.vin_{mfr,model,
                             drive,year,plant,serial}) + native chrome (example, empty state, a11y).

------------------------------------------------------------
STATE COVERAGE (honesty: states reproduced == states that exist in the web source)
------------------------------------------------------------
VinDecoder is a PURE, synchronous, client-side compute tool. Its ONLY data source is `useTranslation`
(the i18n facade, P1/S10); it performs NO network/async/cache work. The web source has exactly two
render branches:
  • empty   — `decoded === null` (VIN < 11 chars) → native: a guiding ContentUnavailableView empty state.
  • decoded — `decoded` truthy → native: the 6-field grid (manufacturer, model, drive, year, plant,
              serial) in the web's insertion order; lookup misses render the localized "Unknown"
              (web `?? t('Unknown')`), an absent serial renders an em dash.
The generic template states loading / error / stale / offline are NOT reachable for a dependency-free
synchronous tool whose only input is the bundled i18n catalog, so they are intentionally NOT
fabricated (covenant #1 no red-as-green, #9 no silent drift). Both real states are implemented and
proven via previews + executed model tests.

`view.opened` diagnostics (P1/S11) emitted once per appearance with slug "VinDecoder" (verified by test).
Accessibility: header marked .isHeader; icons .accessibilityHidden; field carries label+hint; each
decoded cell combines into a single "label: value" element; grid exposes a "Decoded VIN" summary.

